<header><p class="st-kicker">theocracy · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">Ya'aruba dynasty</h1><p class="st-meta">1624 CE – 1744 CE · capital Rustaq</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Omani imamate that expelled the Portuguese from Oman and East Africa and turned Oman into the main naval power of the western Indian Ocean.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1624 Ibadi scholars at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rustaq">Rustaq</a> elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nasir-ibn-murshid">Nasir ibn Murshid al-Ya'rubi</a> as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imam</a>, ending the rule of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/nabhani-dynasty">Nabhani dynasty</a>. He united the interior tribes and attacked the Portuguese coastal forts. His successor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan-ibn-saif">Sultan ibn Saif</a> captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscat">Muscat</a> in 1650, ending <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/portuguese-muscat">Portuguese Muscat</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Ya'aruba built a navy and carried the war to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-africa">East Africa</a>, taking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-jesus">Fort Jesus</a> at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mombasa">Mombasa</a> in 1698 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saif-bin-sultan">Saif ibn Sultan</a> and gaining influence over <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sultanate-of-zanzibar">Zanzibar</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pemba-island">Pemba</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kilwa-sultanate">Kilwa</a>. Trade in slaves, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> and dates enriched the state. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imams</a> built forts and palaces, including the round tower of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nizwa">Nizwa</a> and the palace at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jabrin-castle">Jabrin</a>, and extended falaj irrigation.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>From 1718 disputed successions caused a civil war between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinawi">Hinawi</a> and Ghafiri tribal factions, and one claimant invited Persian forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-ibn-said-al-busaidi">Ahmad ibn Said</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sohar">Sohar</a> expelled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persians">Persians</a> and was elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imam</a> around 1744, founding the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/omani-empire">Omani Empire</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-bu-said-dynasty">Al Bu Said</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/yaaruba-dynasty.jpg" alt="Ya'aruba dynasty" width="320" height="174"><figcaption>Image: Atsuya1 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ya%27ariba_Dynasty%27s_ensign.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1624 CE – 1744 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>theocracy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Rustaq</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Nasir ibn Murshid, Sultan ibn Saif, Saif ibn Sultan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ibadi Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/oman">Oman</a>, <a href="/countries/united-arab-emirates">United Arab Emirates</a>, <a href="/countries/kenya">Kenya</a>, <a href="/countries/tanzania">Tanzania</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Yaruba Imamate, Ya'ariba, Imamate of Oman (1624-1744)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1684&amp;focus=yaaruba-dynasty" aria-label="Ya'aruba dynasty on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6212 1315 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Ya'aruba dynasty lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6532 1571L6533 1657M6532 1571L6562 1563M6532 1571L6298 1144M6532 1571L6562 1563